<mxfile host="Electron" type="device" version="24.7.17" agent="NHSBSA" modified="2026-10-19T09:00:00Z" author="Seamus Sands" organisation="NHSBSA" fit="window">
  <diagram id="08-journey-analyst" name="08-journey-analyst" description="9 steps in rows, each giving where you are in the playbook, what you do and what you produce. 1. Check the playbook applies: Check it applies, then start at Phase 1. Produces: Nothing recorded yet. 2. Phase 1 Engagement and scoping: Agree the decision, the question, what is out of scope, the deadline. Produces: The scope and specification, with the question in one sentence. 3. Deciding your assurance level: Score the impact with your commissioner at scoping. Score the likelihood at design. If an impact dimension scored 4, a full check is not required: it is Level 4 BCA. Produces: The Analytical Assurance Decision Tool, with the Business Critical answer either way. 4. The checks, by level: Read the block for your level and the blocks inside it. Produces: The quality assurance checklist, and your reviewer's time in the schedule. 5. R9 Uncertainty: Find the principal sources of uncertainty while design can still change. Produces: Assumptions listed with their rationale and the impact if wrong. 6. Phase 3 Analysis: Your own verification and validation first, then the critical friend. Produces: The quality assurance log, and what you did about each finding. 7. Phase 4 Delivery, communication and sign-off: State the caveats in the output itself, not only in an annex. Produces: The output and the quality assurance statement, published from Level 3. 8. R10 Data ethics and personal data: Check the Data and AI Ethics Framework, personal data and transparency scope. Produces: The ethics position recorded, and a transparency record drafted where in scope. 9. Phase 5 Review: Ask whether it worked, and whether it is still right. Produces: The review record, the lessons, and any decommissioning decision. Step 3 is outlined: Any one impact dimension at 4? If so, the work is Business Critical. After the last step: What you record at the end is what the next piece of work starts from.">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="680" pageHeight="1004" math="0" shadow="0" background="#F0F4F5">
